                <pb facs="0805" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3241: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-19T17:00:00+08:00">December 19, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 19—8:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Doctor Koo has just asked me to confirm to him a Reuter’s report dated
                    Washington, December 18, to the effect that the United States had addressed a
                    further note to Japan in regard to Manchuria expressing <pb facs="0806" n="696"
                        xml:id="pg696"/> solicitude that Japan’s obligations under the Washington
                    Nine-Power Treaty and the Kellogg-Briand Pact should be respected. Can the
                    Department give me information for Koo?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
